comments.body:
@participant28 as I already mentioned above, please open a new bug report **with a bug report identifier**, noting your app and Android versions, and specifying that it only occurs on Android when MagicDNS is enabled. Provide as many steps as possible to reproduce. If you have multiple devices affected as you mentioned, please attach multiple bug report IDs from each device.

I do want to fix the issue you're experiencing, but the team cannot make sense of what problems users are **_currently_** experiencing when a bug report originally mentioning macOS that is almost two years old gets resurfaced without any recent diagnostic information available. There have been dozens of different MagicDNS fixes since this issue was open, affecting different platforms. For instance, I'm quite sure the issue reported by OP originally was fixed by a change that went into Tailscale 1.58.0. The issue you're seeing on Android has most likely a different root cause, and is likely caused by a custom configuration since the majority of our users are not hitting it. Hence the need for a bug report identifier, so that our team can look at your config too.

We just cannot keep track of _which change fixed which issue_ when very old bug reports keep getting used years later to track issues with different root causes on different platforms. Hope you'll understand.
